e>Ziea</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Wisniewski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Berman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acupuncture for treatment of irritable bowel syndrome</article-title><source>Cochrane Database Syst Rev</source><year>2006</year><volume>18</volume><comment>CD005111</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gates</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Foxcroft</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Auricular acupuncture for cocaine dependence</article-title><source>Cochrane Database Syst Rev</source><year>2006</year><volume>1</volume><comment>CD 005192</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'alberto</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Auricular acupuncture in the treatment of cocaine/crack abuse: a review of the efficacy, the use of the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association protocol, and the selection of sham points</article-title><source>J Altern Complement Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>985</fpage><lpage>1000</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15673993</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lacey</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tershakovec</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acupuncture for the treatment of obesity: a review of the evidence</article-tit